WEBVTT

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:02.448
Possessives and plurals.

00:00:02.448 --> 00:00:04.313
Apostrophes show ownership.

00:00:04.313 --> 00:00:05.731
They never make plurals.

00:00:07.277 --> 00:00:09.027
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:09.027 --> 00:00:13.327
The choices are the same word, with the apostrophe moved around.

00:00:13.327 --> 00:00:16.413
And the word is usually followed by something it might own.

00:00:17.426 --> 00:00:20.617
It's testing whether you can tell a plural from a possessive.

00:00:21.644 --> 00:00:22.944
Here's the method.

00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:25.669
Ask: does this word own the next word?

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:27.509
If not, no apostrophe.

00:00:27.509 --> 00:00:29.669
Is there one owner, or many?

00:00:29.669 --> 00:00:31.069
Look for clues.

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:33.419
One owner gets apostrophe s.

00:00:33.419 --> 00:00:35.644
Many owners get s apostrophe.

00:00:35.644 --> 00:00:39.398
And pronouns like its, their, and whose never take an apostrophe.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.278
Rule one: a plain plural is just s.

00:00:43.278 --> 00:00:45.928
If nothing is owned, there's no apostrophe.

00:00:45.928 --> 00:00:47.119
The plants bloom.

00:00:48.206 --> 00:00:52.056
Rule two: many owners take s, then the apostrophe.

00:00:52.056 --> 00:00:54.401
The campaign belongs to many residents.

00:00:55.473 --> 00:00:59.473
Rule three: words like children and women are already plural.

00:00:59.473 --> 00:01:01.973
So it's not childrens, apostrophe.

00:01:01.973 --> 00:01:04.259
It's children, apostrophe s.

00:01:05.314 --> 00:01:06.539
Let's try one.

00:01:06.539 --> 00:01:08.389
Does the word own the next one?

00:01:08.389 --> 00:01:12.179
The campaign belongs to the residents, so yes, it's possessive.

00:01:12.179 --> 00:01:13.899
One resident, or many?

00:01:13.899 --> 00:01:15.899
A whole campaign means many.

00:01:15.899 --> 00:01:18.039
A has no apostrophe at all.

00:01:18.039 --> 00:01:20.064
B means just one resident.

00:01:20.064 --> 00:01:22.189
D isn't standard English.

00:01:22.189 --> 00:01:24.774
Many owners: s, then the apostrophe.

00:01:24.774 --> 00:01:26.103
The answer is C.

00:01:27.173 --> 00:01:29.648
Watch out for the plural apostrophe.

00:01:29.648 --> 00:01:32.578
If nothing is owned, there's no apostrophe.

00:01:32.578 --> 00:01:34.913
The dog's barked all night is wrong.

00:01:34.913 --> 00:01:36.099
Just the dogs.

00:01:37.144 --> 00:01:39.014
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:39.014 --> 00:01:40.074
How to spot it.

00:01:40.074 --> 00:01:41.424
The four steps.

00:01:41.424 --> 00:01:42.529
The rules.

00:01:42.529 --> 00:01:43.554
And the trap.

00:01:43.554 --> 00:01:46.313
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
